!**************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
!Reaction Mechanism of ethyl acetate (EA) in CHEMKIN format                                                                                                                
!Title: Experimental and Kinetic Modeling Study of Ethyl Acetate Pyrolysis and Oxidation in a Shock Tube                                                                           
!A new detailed kinetic mechanism is developed by integrating the C0–C4 framework from NUIG Mech 1.1. and key sub-frameworks for EA, CH3COOH, and CH2CO from the Morsch and Sun models. 
!five elementary reactions were identified as key rate-controlling steps for both EA oxidation and pyrolysis,and reaction rate constants was updated: 
!CH3COOH<=>CO2+CH4, CH3COOH<=>CH2CO+H2O, CH3COOH<=>CH3+COOH, CH2CO+H<=>CH3+CO, and C2H4+OH<=>C2H3+H2O

!! please cite as:
!Y. Wu, S. Panigrahy, A.B. Sahu, C. Bariki, J. Beeckmann, J. Liang, A.A. Mohamed, S. Dong, C. Tang, H. Pitsch, Understanding the antagonistic effect of methanol as a component in surrogate fuel models: A case study of methanol/n-heptane mixtures, Combust. Flame 226 (2021) 229-242.
!P. Morsch, M. Döntgen, K. Heufer, Kinetic investigations on the high-and low-temperature chemistry of ethyl acetate, Combust. Flame 243 (2022) 111995.
!W. Sun, T. Tao, R. Zhang, H. Liao, C. Huang, F. Zhang, X. Zhang, Y. Zhang, B. Yang, Experimental and modeling efforts towards a better understanding of the high-temperature combustion kinetics of C3C5 ethyl esters, Combust. Flame 185 (2017) 173-187.
!A. Elwardany, E.F. Nasir, E. Es-sebbar, A. Farooq, Unimolecular decomposition of formic and acetic acids: A shock tube/laser absorption study, Proc. Combust. Inst. 35 (2015) 429-436.
!F. Šlemr, P. Warneck, Reactions of atomic hydrogen with ketene and acetaldehyde, Ber. Bunsen-Ges. Phys. Chem. Chem. Phys. 79 (1975) 152-156.
!S.S. Vasu, Z. Hong, D.F. Davidson, R.K. Hanson, D.M. Golden, Shock tube/laser absorption measurements of the reaction rates of OH with ethylene and propene, J. Phys. Chem. A 114 (2010) 11529-11537.
!**************************************************************************************************************************************************************************


